.emergent/

# Exception: track only the R5 Capability Platform spec phase directory
# (requirements.md/design.md/tasks.md + any later OWNERSHIP.md/MIGRATION-PLAN.md/
# ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md/CLOSURE-NOTES.md living alongside them). All other
# .kiro content (other spec phases, frontend/docs/) remains ignored — each
# level below is re-ignored via a wildcard before the next level is opened,
# so only the one named path is ever un-ignored.
!frontend/.kiro/
frontend/.kiro/*
!frontend/.kiro/specs/
frontend/.kiro/specs/*
!frontend/.kiro/specs/R5-capability-platform/
!frontend/.kiro/specs/R5-capability-platform/**
# R7 Clinical Operating System: track the approved, frozen R7 specification
# package (requirements.md v1.0 FROZEN, design.md v1.0 APPROVED, tasks.md
# APPROVED, plus the supporting ratification/design/state documents) —
# mirrors the R5-capability-platform exception above.
!frontend/.kiro/specs/R7-guided-clinical-workspace/
!frontend/.kiro/specs/R7-guided-clinical-workspace/**
# ED-ARCH-001 finding: also track frontend/.kiro/engineering/ — general,
# non-phase-specific governance records (ENGINEERING-DEBT.md and any future
# ENGINEERING-TRUTH.md), mirroring the backend repo's own
# .kiro/engineering/ exception. Must be tracked: engineering debt is
# explicitly required to be part of the project's tracked record.
!frontend/.kiro/engineering/
!frontend/.kiro/engineering/**
